{"id": "85946", "name": "כלל השרשרת – (1−xᵐ)ⁿ (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Differentiate {{CT:0}} with respect to {{CT:1}}.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> The function is a composition \\(f(g(x))\\) of an outer function and an inner function \\(g\\); by the chain rule its derivative is the derivative of the outer function, evaluated at \\(g\\), times the derivative of the inner function.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The inner and outer functions</b><br>In order to solve this problem we will have to use the chain rule as follows:<div style=\"background:#FFF8E6;border:1px solid #E8D29A;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0\">The chain rule: \\( \\frac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=f'(g(x))\\,g'(x) \\)</div><p>Define \\(f({{CT:2}})={{CT:3}}\\) and \\(g({{CT:2}})={{CT:4}}\\).</p><p>So \\(f({{CT:2}})=g({{CT:2}})^{{CT:5}}\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Differentiating</b><br>So,<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\begin{array}{rcl}\\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}[{{CT:3}}] &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle \\frac{df}{dg}\\cdot \\frac{dg}{d{{CT:2}}} \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle \\frac{d}{dg}(g^{{CT:5}})\\cdot \\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}({{CT:4}}) \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle {{CT:5}}g^{{{CT:5}}-1}\\cdot (-{{CT:6}}){{CT:2}}^{{{CT:6}}-1} \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle -{{CT:7}}{{CT:2}}^{{CT:8}}({{CT:4}})^{{CT:9}} \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle -{{CT:10}} \\end{array} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "w1:1+v^rdm1;\nw2:w1^rdm2;", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Diff", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(w2,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You appear to have lost a minus sign and differentiated {@w2@} instead of {{CT:0}}.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "Result-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "-diff(p,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Check your signs, your answer is the negative of what it should be.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "Result-2-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 3, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)/diff(pp,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-3-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p>You need to use the chain rule so that</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}[f(g(x))]=\\frac{df}{dg}\\cdot \\frac{dg}{dx}\\]</p><p>but you have not included the \\(\\frac{dg}{dx}\\) term.</p></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-3-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["p", "pp", "rdm1", "rdm2", "v"], "nvariants": 15}